Vikram and Betal: The Wise Decision (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100139

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there were two friends who found a purse full of money,” said Betal. “Both wanted to keep it.”

They started arguing over who should take it.

Finally, they went to a wise elder for help.

The elder listened to both of them.

He said, “Let us wait here. The real owner might come looking for it.”

After some time, a worried man came searching for his lost purse.

He described it correctly.

The elder gave the purse back to him.

The two friends felt ashamed.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what made the elder wise?”

Vikram replied, “He chose patience and fairness instead of rushing.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Patience and fairness lead to the right decision.
